{
  "$meta": {
    "name": "LUZ Design System",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Consistent · Adaptive · Identity",
    "scales": "Spacing: a 2px hairline, then the 4px unit (0.25rem) times 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24 (each power of two and its 1.5x half step). Control heights: 44px (the WCAG 2.5.5 target) and steps of 1.25x around it, on the 4px grid. Type: the readability floors 12, 14 and 15px, the 16px base, then x1.25 per step, each step rounded to 1/16 rem (1px at the default). The base, the ratio and the space unit are the knobs --luz-type-base, --luz-type-ratio and --luz-space-unit: set them on :root.",
    "color": "LUZ's own palette, computed in OKLCH by scripts/build-palette.js. Edit that script, not these values."
  },
